You feel spoiled.

	Intrinsics are more or less permanent.  They can be lost (due
to a gremlin attack) but they don't fade or wear out.  The exception
to this is if a temple priest gives you Clairvoyance.  In that case,
Clairvoyance will wear off after {mumble} turns.

>Also, how do you distinguish weapon effectiveness with any accuracy?

	The best way I can think of is to find a platoon of orcs and
figure out how long it takes to off one, on the average.  Reading a
scroll of identify over it will give you great insight into the
enchantments laid on the weapon, but it won't tell you whether a
glaive is any better than a ranseur.  My strategy is usually to hold
on to the weapon I start with until I find a good named weapon.

>Are all your scores listed at the bottom of the screen? (Besides
>intrinsics.)

	No, there are a few things the game tracks that don't appear
there, such as Alignment and Luck.  You can get a general idea of your
Alignment (high/medium/low) by applying a stethoscope to yourself, or
by quaffing a potion of enlightenment.  There is no sure way of
knowing your Luck, except by making educated guesses.

>My stats have been increasing due to physical labor, will they go
>down if I rest a lot?

	No, they only go down if something happens to indicate they
might be compromised.  Hallucinating, starving, vomiting, and injuring
one's legs are a few of the instances which might cause one's stats to
decrease.

